# --- report assets -----------------------------------------------------------
# Tarballs from the cluster figure-asset pull (docs/pull-figure-assets.md). The
# unpacked HTML under report/assets/ is small and IS tracked, so the figures stay
# reproducible from a clone; the archive itself is not.
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Deliberately NOT ignored, so a fresh clone can rebuild the submission:
#   report/figures/*.png              generated, but data.zip is ignored, so a
#                                      clone could not otherwise show them
#   report/assets/glyphs.npz          the 0.07 MB glyph input, extracted from data.zip
#   report/assets/model_output/       real model-output SVGs pulled off the cluster
#                                      (docs/pull-figure-assets.md), 24 small HTML files
#   report/assets/model_output_l1.csv per-glyph L1 over that pull (rank_failures.py,
#                                      cluster-only, needs cairosvg)
#   report/assets/model_output_renders.npz  rasterized crops of the above
#                                      (render_model_output.py, cluster-only,
#                                      needs cairosvg) -- committed so
#                                      make_model_comparison_figures.py needs
#                                      nothing beyond numpy on the Mac
#   report/REPORT.pdf                 the deliverable itself

# Papers. Linked from README.md rather than vendored: they are large, they are not
# ours to redistribute, and arXiv is a more durable address than a git blob.
DeepVecFontV2.pdf
DeepVecFont v1.pdf
FinalProjectPart2.pdf

# Staging area for removal. This sandbox cannot delete files on the Mac, so anything
# retired gets moved here and Ben removes the folder himself. Never tracked.
_to_delete/
